SQL> SELECT branch, COUNT(*) FROM students GROUP BY branch;
+--------+----------+
| branch | COUNT(*) |
+--------+----------+
| CSE    |        2 |
| ECE    |        2 |
| IT     |        2 |
+--------+----------+
3 rows in set

SQL> SELECT branch, AVG(cgpa) FROM students GROUP BY branch HAVING AVG(cgpa) > 8;
+--------+-----------+
| branch | AVG(cgpa) |
+--------+-----------+
| CSE    |       8.8 |
| ECE    |      9.15 |
+--------+-----------+
2 rows in set

